# Compose-level settings. Copy to deploy/.env (deploy.sh does this on first run).
# Read by `docker compose` for interpolation ONLY — nothing in this file reaches
# the application containers (those read deploy/app.env). Secrets live as files
# under deploy/secrets/ (generated by deploy.sh) and are never written here.
# NEVER commit .env.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which compose files make up the stack (colon-separated overlays on the base):
#   docker-compose.prod.yml                                   public server
#   docker-compose.lan.yml                                    LAN test box (dev only, plain HTTP)
#   docker-compose.prod.yml:docker-compose.monitoring.yml     + logs/metrics/alerts
#   docker-compose.prod.yml:docker-compose.wal-archive.yml    + WAL archiving (PITR)
COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.prod.yml

# Image tag to run. deploy.sh sets this from `git rev-parse --short HEAD` on
# every deploy; set it here (or on the command line) only to pin/roll back.
#IMAGE_TAG=abc1234

# Site address for Caddy:
#   payments.example.com  automatic public HTTPS (needs DNS + 80/443 open) + HSTS
#   192.168.1.156         bare IP: Caddy issues a cert from its internal CA;
#                         trust the root (see README "Internal CA")
#   :80                   plain HTTP — smoke tests only, never real traffic
SITE_ADDRESS=:80

# REQUIRED — who may reach the admin surface: the /admin console AND the admin
# API (/v1/admin/*, /v1/deposits*, KYC approve/reject). Space-separated
# IPs/CIDRs (your office / VPN egress). Everyone else gets 403 at Caddy.
# deploy.sh refuses to deploy while this is unset. To knowingly expose the
# admin surface to the whole internet (not recommended) write: 0.0.0.0/0 ::/0
#ADMIN_ALLOW_CIDR=203.0.113.7/32 10.8.0.0/24

# Number of payment-server replicas. Caddy gets one upstream per replica and
# health-checks each on /ready, so a replica that loses the database leaves
# rotation on its own. Keep replicas x DB_MAX_CONNECTIONS + ~20 below 200.
#API_REPLICAS=1

# Group id that may read deploy/secrets/* (files are 0640, group SECRETS_GID;
# every container that is handed a secret runs with this supplementary group).
# Pick an id no real group on the host uses.
#SECRETS_GID=10500

# --- backups ---
# Daily dump / KYC archive times (HH:MM, UTC).
#BACKUP_DB_AT=02:00
#BACKUP_KYC_AT=02:30
# Encryption of dumps and KYC archives. `auto` (default) encrypts to whatever
# deploy/secrets/backup_recipients holds: age recipients (deploy.sh generates
# an age key pair on first run) or an ASCII-armoured OpenPGP public key.
# `none` is refused for production and only allowed with the LAN overlay.
#BACKUP_ENCRYPTION=auto
# Optional off-box copy after every backup: an rclone remote path, defined in
# deploy/secrets/backup_rclone_conf (e.g. an S3/B2 bucket or an SFTP host).
# The files are already encrypted; set retention as a bucket lifecycle rule.
#BACKUP_OFFSITE_REMOTE=offsite:payment-backups/prod

# --- LAN overlay only (docker-compose.lan.yml) ---
# The LAN address the console (8088) and the API (8099) are published on.
# Required by the overlay; never 0.0.0.0 on a box with a public interface.
#LAN_BIND_ADDRESS=192.168.1.156

# --- monitoring overlay only (docker-compose.monitoring.yml) ---
# Grafana admin password (bound to 127.0.0.1:3000; reach it over an SSH tunnel).
# Required by the overlay — no default.
#GRAFANA_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
# Where Alertmanager POSTs alerts (ntfy topic, Slack/Mattermost bridge, PagerDuty
# events API, ...). Required by the overlay — no default.
#ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://ntfy.sh/CHANGE_ME_topic
# Dead man's switch: Alertmanager pings this URL every minute while the
# always-firing Watchdog alert flows (healthchecks.io / Cronitor / Dead Man's
# Snitch check URL). That service must page you when the pings STOP — it is
# the only alert that can report the whole box being down. Required.
#ALERT_HEARTBEAT_URL=https://hc-ping.com/CHANGE_ME-uuid
